      "0": [
        {
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 25 (URL: https://app.slack.com/client/T064SFP56MC/C08DJTEFUSX, Title: \"feedback-and-ideas (Channel) - Daytona Community - Slack\"). In the visible channel message list under \"Channel feedback-and-ideas\", the DOM shows exactly 4 substantive proposal-like posts: \n1) \"Matthew Jones 11:11 AM\" with text \"are there plans to have the Otel frequency adjustable?\" and thread metadata \"7 replies, Last reply 3 months ago\" plus evidence timestamp \"May 13th at 11:11:51 AM\".\n2) \"Ramon Garate 1:14 PM\" with text \"feedback: maybe this error message could be improved? Error …\" and thread metadata \"1 reply, 3 months ago\" plus evidence timestamp \"May 27th at 1:14:41 PM\".\n3) \"Liren Peng 6:50 PM\" with text \"Hi Daytona team, …\" and thread metadata \"2 replies, Last reply 3 months ago\" plus evidence timestamp \"May 28th at 6:50:25 PM\".\n4) \"TEN 11:38 PM\" with a long suggestion post beginning \"Hi Daytona Support Team, I’ve been exploring Daytona... I have a few suggestions...\" and evidence timestamp \"Jun 5th at 11:38:14 PM\".\nThe DOM also shows a history limitation banner: \"View messages and files older than 90 days... Messages and files on the free version of Slack are hidden after 90 days.\" and a jump control \"From May 28th, 2026 and older\".\nAdditionally, the DOM shows one opened thread panel: \"Thread in feedback-and-ideas (channel, 7 replies)\" for \"Michael Xu Jul 6th at 2:46 PM\" with message text about network egress controls and \"fixed egress IP\", and explicit reaction evidence lines \"1 reaction, react with eyes emoji\" and \"1 reaction, react with white check mark emoji\".",
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe criterion requires inspecting up to the 10 most recent substantive proposals in #feedback-and-ideas, and if fewer exist/are available, analyzing all available and stating the limitation.\n\nSupported aspects from DOM state 25:\n- The agent is in the correct channel: the page title and header show \"feedback-and-ideas\" and the URL is the Slack client with channel id C08DJTEFUSX.\n- The DOM visibly contains (at least) four proposal-like messages in the main channel list (Matthew Jones, Ramon Garate, Liren Peng, TEN), each with visible author and some thread metadata. This demonstrates the agent had access to and could inspect multiple proposals.\n- The DOM contains an explicit limitation about message visibility/history: \"Messages and files on the free version of Slack are hidden after 90 days\" plus a control \"From May 28th, 2026 and older\". This is direct evidence that not all history may be available, which could justify analyzing fewer than 10 if only a subset is visible.\n\nWhy only PARTIAL:\n- The DOM evidence does not show that the agent inspected (or even had visible) up to 10 *most recent* substantive proposals; it only shows 4 proposals in the main list plus a separate opened thread for Michael Xu. There is no DOM evidence in state 25 for additional proposals (e.g., Lukas Seufert, Gautam Talks, Rob Schoening, Liudmila Joukovskaya) that were claimed in the agent’s produced summary; they are not present in the visible channel list in this snapshot.\n- Therefore, while the channel was accessed and some proposals were visible/inspectable, the requirement to inspect up to 10 most recent proposals is only partially evidenced by the DOM snapshot (4 in list + 1 open thread), and the “10 most recent” scope is not verifiable from the provided DOM alone.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s predicted summary claims inspection of 10 proposals including Rob Schoening, Liudmila Joukovskaya, Lukas Seufert, Gautam Talks, and others with specific reply/reaction counts. In DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX:25, the visible main channel list only shows four posts (Matthew Jones, Ramon Garate, Liren Peng, TEN) plus an open thread for Michael Xu. No DOM evidence in this snapshot supports the existence/visibility of the additional named proposals or their reaction/reply counts at the time of analysis. Also, the agent summary asserts \"Messages older than 90 days are hidden\"—this is supported by the banner text, but it is not sufficient to substantiate the specific older posts/counted reactions that are not present in the DOM snapshot.",
