        {
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 14 shows the agent is in Slack channel “feedback-and-ideas” (Title: “feedback-and-ideas (Channel) - Daytona Community - Slack”, URL https://app.slack.com/client/T064SFP56MC/C08DJTEFUSX). In the visible message list it contains at least four substantive proposal/feedback posts:\n- “Matthew Jones 11:11 AM” with text “are there plans to have the Otel frequency adjustable?” and “thread: 7 replies, Last reply 3 months ago” (evidence: “May 13th at 11:11:51 AM”).\n- “Ramon Garate 1:14 PM” with text “feedback: maybe this error message could be improved? Error …” and “thread: 1 reply, 3 months ago” (evidence: “May 27th at 1:14:41 PM”).\n- “Liren Peng 6:50 PM” with text “Hi Daytona team, …” and “thread: 2 replies, Last reply 3 months ago” (evidence: “May 28th at 6:50:25 PM”).\n- “TEN 11:38 PM” with a long message starting “Hi Daytona Support Team, I’ve been exploring Daytona…” (evidence: “Jun 5th at 11:38:14 PM”).\nAdditionally, the UI shows an access limitation banner: “View messages and files older than 90 days… Messages and files on the free version of Slack are hidden after 90 days.”\nThe right-side thread panel is open for a substantive feature request by “Michael Xu Jul 6th at 2:46 PM” beginning “hey everyone - feature request…” and includes “evidence: 1 reaction, react with eyes emoji” and “evidence: 1 reaction, react with white check mark emoji”, plus “Thread in feedback-and-ideas (channel, 7 replies)” and visible replies from “Dalin Stone Jul 6th at 3:07 PM” including “No we do not have this yet, but there is a workaround using tailscale” and a longer explanation “How we support static egress IPs: The recommended approach is to use a VPN connection with Tailscale…”",
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe criterion requires inspecting up to the 10 most recent substantive proposals in #feedback-and-ideas, or all available/visible if fewer exist, and explicitly stating limitations.\n\nSupported aspects: DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 14 confirms the agent navigated to #feedback-and-ideas and that multiple substantive proposal-like posts are visible (Matthew Jones’ Otel frequency question; Ramon Garate’s error-message improvement feedback; Liren Peng’s general feedback; TEN’s multi-suggestion DX post). It also shows a concrete limitation that older history may be hidden (“Messages and files… hidden after 90 days”), which is relevant to explaining why fewer than 10 may be accessible.\n\nWhy only PARTIAL: The DOM snapshot evidences visibility/inspection of only a handful of proposals in the channel list (4) plus one thread open (Michael Xu). It does not evidence that the agent inspected “up to the 10 most recent” proposals because (a) only a small subset is visible in the captured DOM, and (b) there is no DOM evidence of navigating/scrolling to enumerate up to 10 recent proposals beyond what’s shown. Therefore, while channel access and inspection of some proposals is supported, inspection completeness up to 10 (or confirmation that fewer exist/are accessible) is not fully proven by the DOM state alone.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s produced answer lists 10 proposals (including Rob Schoening, Liudmila Joukovskaya, Lukas Seufert, Gautam Talks, and a Daytona spot GPU announcement) with reaction/reply counts. None of those additional items (beyond Matthew Jones, Ramon Garate, Liren Peng, TEN, and the Michael Xu thread) appear in DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 14, and the DOM shows a 90-day history hiding banner that could prevent viewing older content. Thus, the DOM evidence does not support the claim that 10 recent proposals were actually inspected/visible in this run.",
